@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About - OS Arkiv</PageTitle>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">About the archive</div>
        <h1 class="section__title" style="margin-top:0.5rem; max-width:16ch;">An archive of clothes that were otherwise discarded</h1>

        <div class="split-grid">
            <div class="prose">
                <p>
                    OS Arkiv started as a small workshop with one sewing machine and a pile of
                    clothes nobody else wanted. Today it's a catalogue of reworked clothing —
                    every piece inspected, repaired or resewn, and given a number in the archive.
                </p>
                <p>
                    We don't design around seasonal trends. We design around the fabric in front
                    of us — a discarded jacket, three shirts from a clothing swap, the offcuts
                    from another designer's pattern-cutting. That means no two pieces are alike,
                    and the archive keeps changing.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Everything is sewn and reworked in our own workshop. We believe clothing that
                    already exists is the most sustainable material there is.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="split-grid__image">
                <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/os-arkiv-about/900/1150" alt="From the OS Arkiv workshop" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
